1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:31,406
<i>You need to leave!</i>
<i>You have to get out of here!</i>

6
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:35,326
<i>Just to repeat myself!</i>
<i>I bought this space!</i>

7
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:38,455
<i>Therefore, you're trespassing! Get out!</i>

8
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:39,581
[Mercedes] <i>Madam.</i>

9
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:42,876
<i>Lily Cruz has the</i>
<i>people of Ardiente behind her.</i>

10
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,420
<i>It's about time we let her know</i>

11
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:47,255
<i>that you're not to be messed with.</i>

12
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:50,133
-[Mateo] <i>What is this?</i>
-[Jaguar] <i>Emilia Ardiente.</i>

13
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,886
<i>I just want you to know that she's mine.</i>

14
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:56,806
<i>If you want this partnership</i>
<i>to last, tell off your allies.</i>

15
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:57,891
<i>Who are you talking about?</i>

16
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>-Why don't you ask Jaguar?</i>
<i>-Ma'am, sir! It's Mr. Arnaldo.</i>

17
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,687
<i>Why? What happened to my grandson?</i>

18
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:05,690
-[Julio] <i>Arnaldo? Arnaldo!</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Arnaldo.</i>

19
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:06,858
<i>Who are you?</i>

20
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:09,277
[doctor] <i>Arnaldo is suffering</i>
<i>from retrograde amnesia.</i>

21
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,988
[reporter] <i>Six condominium</i>
<i>buildings and a media complex</i>

22
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:13,364
<i>owned by Aguas Realty</i>

23
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,657
<i>were bombed earlier this morning</i>

24
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:18,203
<i>in what could be the deadliest</i>
<i>terrorist attack in recent memory.</i>

25
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:21,915
<i>Aguas Realty is done for,</i>
<i>and it's all your fault.</i>

26
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:26,127
<i>They may have destroyed our</i>
<i>buildings, but never our spirit.</i>

27
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:29,464
<i>We will rise again,</i>
<i>and we will be the symbol</i>

28
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:32,509
<i>of strength, courage, and hope.</i>

29
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:34,886
[Julio] <i>Whoever is behind these bombings</i>

30
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:40,183
<i>is giving Lily Cruz victory</i>
<i>on a silver platter!</i>

31
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:41,351
<i>Diego, do you remember</i>

32
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:43,228
<i>that woman at the construction site?</i>

33
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:45,271
<i>I believe she's our key</i>

34
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:47,649
<i>to finding out who's behind the bombings.</i>

35
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:52,612
Any updates on what I told you to do?

36
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:56,324
Boss Jaguar, the bombing
of Aguas Realty was a clean job.

37
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:58,493
We still don't know
who's responsible for it,

38
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:01,412
but they used high-powered explosives.

39
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:04,207
I know one person
who could've masterminded…

40
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:06,334
a large-scale attack like that.

41
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:11,089
Boss Jaguar, I think the
Red Dragon is spitting out fire.

42
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,467
[tense music playing]

43
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:16,761
Has she contacted you again?

44
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:20,849
You may leave.

45
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:22,725
I'll call you again if I need anything.

46
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:29,107
[tense music intensifies]

47
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:34,863
Please call Arnaldo.

48
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:35,989
Yes, sir.

49
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:40,577
Governor. You called for me?

50
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:46,166
Yeah. I want you to monitor
Emilia very closely.

51
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:53,006
I suspect she's involved in the bombings

52
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:56,676
of Lily Cruz's properties.
I have this funny feeling

53
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:59,679
that my daughter
is hiding something from us.

54
00:03:00,054 --> 00:03:01,973
-Yes, Governor.
-Thank you.

55
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:05,894
[laughing] He is so annoying!

56
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:07,854
You know, Papa just laughed
the whole thing off.

57
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:11,107
But I know Mama is involved
in the bombings.

58
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:14,485
I'd rather not comment on the issue.

59
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:17,822
That's a nice PR answer.
Can you at least, like,

60
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:21,951
blink once if it's a yes,
or blink twice if it's a no?

61
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,871
All I can say is that your mother

62
00:03:24,954 --> 00:03:26,247
is paving the way for you.

63
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:29,208
So, just try to be
a little more patient, Emilia.

64
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:34,589
[clicks tongue] I'm an Ardiente.
Patience is a virtue.

65
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:38,301
Or should I say, a talent
that I never learned?

66
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,804
You are much more than an Ardiente, madam.

67
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:43,556
You're way, way more.

68
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:46,267
So, just try to be patient and trust me.

69
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:47,810
[inhales]

70
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:50,897
[exhales] Okay, I will try my best.

71
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,607
My very, very best.

72
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:57,153
[tense music playing]

73
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:08,539
[Julio] Hmm.

74
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:10,083
-Thank you.
-Arnaldo.

75
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:11,626
Sit down. Sit down, please.

76
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:12,502
Sure.

77
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:17,882
Uh… It's been a while
since we shared a meal together.

78
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:20,176
-[Arnaldo chuckles]
-And look at what we have.

79
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,804
So, let us partake of this full--

80
00:04:22,887 --> 00:04:23,805
[Arnaldo sniffles]

81
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:27,642
-Amen. Yeah.
-Amen.

82
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:29,727
Um…

83
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:32,563
Yeah, as I was saying, um…
we have good food.

84
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:34,440
So, let's dig in.

85
00:04:34,774 --> 00:04:36,276
Okay. [chuckles]

86
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:37,735
[Julio exhales]

87
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:39,195
You know, I…

88
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:46,202
I noticed a lot of changes
in you since you woke up

89
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,288
from your coma.

90
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:50,123
Um…

91
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:51,958
Is everything all right?

92
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:53,751
Is everything all right with you?

93
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,212
Uh… Of course, Grandpa.

94
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,840
Everything's all right.
I've never felt better.

95
00:04:59,507 --> 00:05:04,220
You know, it's like a heavy load
was lifted from my heart.

96
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,264
[soft music playing]

97
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,683
I can't remember the past, but…

98
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:11,811
I'm excited about the future.

99
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:15,064
[clicks tongue] Now, that is good to hear,

100
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:16,524
that you're excited about the future.

101
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:17,608
[Arnaldo] Yes.

102
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,819
-So, um…
-[Arnaldo sniffles]

103
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:26,743
Just tell me when you feel you're ready,

104
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:33,166
so we can start planning
your return to politics.

105
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,709
Hmm.

106
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,253
Uh…

107
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,050
I want to quit politics, Grandpa.

108
00:05:46,721 --> 00:05:48,723
Um… [clears throat]

109
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:52,894
Well… if you want to quit politics,

110
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,187
what do you want to do?

111
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,524
-Well, I want to be a priest.
-[chokes]

112
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:00,735
-Sir, are you okay?
-[Julio coughing]

113
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:02,779
Calm down. I'm okay. I'm okay.

114
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,072
[Julio clears throat]

115
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:06,449
-Are you okay? Sure?
-Yeah, yeah.

116
00:06:06,532 --> 00:06:08,534
Yes, I'm--I'm okay.

117
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:10,661
-[clears throat]
-Okay.

118
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:14,582
-Let's eat.
-Yeah.

119
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:19,921
[sighs]

120
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:22,006
Remember Helena Montoya?

121
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:27,011
Yes. The philanthropist who
wants to invest in our company.

122
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:29,931
I want to review her proposal first.

123
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:31,182
Okay.

124
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:33,810
I also know an investor

125
00:06:33,893 --> 00:06:35,978
who's interested
in investing in Aguas Realty.

126
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,647
Who?

127
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:41,943
I'll talk to them first,
then I'll give you the details.

128
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:45,321
They have to go through me, Mr. Paterno.

129
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:48,616
[tense music playing]

130
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,701
[sighs]

131
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:52,703
Miss Cruz…

132
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:57,291
I am not a freaking amateur.

133
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,837
I can handle this.

134
00:07:06,884 --> 00:07:08,219
Mr. Paterno…

135
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,889
I don't think it would hurt for me…

136
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:15,977
to be cautious and inspect
every transaction we make here,

137
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:21,065
because I don't know who wants
to tear my company down.

138
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:23,484
-I know what I'm doing.
-No!

139
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:30,283
I want all the details about your investor

140
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:32,493
on my table tomorrow…

141
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:36,080
before the meeting begins.

142
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:39,542
[tense music playing]

143
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:46,674
Like what you said, Mr. Paterno,
you're not an amateur.

144
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:50,178
Details. Tomorrow.

145
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:57,602
[tense music intensifies]

146
00:08:01,355 --> 00:08:05,651
Doc, you have to explain this to me.

147
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,863
Is my grandson ill, huh?

148
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:12,158
Why does he want to be a priest?

149
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,327
Is the kid really going nuts?

150
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:18,748
Your grandson is experiencing
dissociative fugue.

151
00:08:19,081 --> 00:08:23,669
Because of his memory loss,
his brain is manifesting

152
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:26,297
a new consciousness to fill in the blanks.

153
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:30,551
It created a new identity…

154
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:33,721
that is totally different
from his inherent personality.

155
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:41,103
So, in short, my grandson
has really gone bonkers.

156
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:43,397
Doctor…

157
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:49,529
I've trained that child
since he was a little boy.

158
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:54,367
I trained him to be the fiercest
ruler among all Ardientes.

159
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:57,537
And now, this is what's
going to happen to him?

160
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,831
No! No. You have to help me, doc.

161
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:03,751
We need to bring the old Arnaldo back.

162
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:06,003
-[Arnaldo] Amen?
-[workers] Amen.

163
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:10,591
What? What was that?

164
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:13,928
[soft music playing]

165
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:14,929
[Arnaldo] Okay.

166
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:20,393
Next time, I'll read something
I'm sure that you'll all love.

167
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:23,062
-[Julio] Hey.
-Grandpa?

168
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:25,064
Um, good evening, Arnaldo.

169
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:26,190
[Arnaldo] Good evening.

170
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:30,528
All right, everybody, back to your posts.

171
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:31,988
Let's go.

172
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:33,531
Let's do this again next week. Okay?

173
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:41,998
Doc, we're good for now.
I'll talk to my grandson.

174
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:43,624
-Okay, Governor.
-Thank you.

175
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:50,881
Arnaldo…

176
00:09:52,258 --> 00:09:58,014
I want you to stop preaching religion

177
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:59,515
to everyone here.

178
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,643
This isn't like you.
You're confusing them.

179
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:07,189
You have to return to your old self!

180
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:09,317
But I'm no longer the Arnaldo

181
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,401
-you once knew.
-[scoffs]

182
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:13,112
Grandpa, the old Arnaldo is gone.

183
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:18,576
The old has gone, and the new has come.

184
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,954
And right now, this is
the new Arnaldo, Grandpa.

185
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:26,083
Cut it out. The Arnaldo that I know…

186
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:30,421
is the mayor of Poblacion, Ardiente.

187
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:35,509
The Arnaldo that I remember is
someone I trained to be brave.

188
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:39,180
And when someone gets
in his way, he kills them.

189
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:43,351
You will go back to your old self,

190
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,478
to the Arnaldo that I remember.

191
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,106
So, you better stop this nonsense.

192
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:52,360
Or else, you'll see what I can do!

193
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:56,447
[dramatic music playing]

194
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,791
[phone chimes]

195
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:10,544
Hello?

196
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,755
[tense music playing]

197
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:14,548
Get ready for your next mission.

198
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:23,557
[tense music intensifies]

199
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:30,606
[thumps]

200
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:33,818
That Lily Cruz is so full of herself!

201
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:37,530
Who does she think she is? [sighs]

202
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:42,701
If I didn't owe so much to Prianka,
I would've left this company long ago.

203
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:47,123
To think, I'm trying to save this company!

204
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:48,791
She's such an ingrate.

205
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,209
So, what now?

206
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:52,378
Will you still give information
about your investor?

207
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,172
Me, give her information?

208
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:58,175
Of course not! You know what she'll do?

209
00:11:58,259 --> 00:12:01,429
She'll get the investor
and take the credit!

210
00:12:02,471 --> 00:12:03,639
[sighs]

211
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:05,641
[phone rings]

212
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:09,728
Excuse me. I need to answer this call.

213
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:10,813
Sure.

214
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:15,317
-[ringing continues]
-[sighs]

215
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:19,947
Mercedes?

216
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:24,034
Mr. Paterno. Have you talked to Lily Cruz?

217
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:28,497
Has our investment in
Aguas Realty been approved?

218
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:30,875
Uh… I'm sorry.

219
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:32,501
We just had a little trouble here.

220
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,628
<i>But don't worry. I got you.</i>

221
00:12:34,712 --> 00:12:37,381
Just keep your word that
you'll invest a huge amount.

222
00:12:39,258 --> 00:12:40,468
<i>After all the bombings,</i>

223
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:44,263
Aguas Realty is still a good investment.

224
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:46,765
The people still trust our company.

225
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:50,102
Very well then. My associate
will meet you tomorrow.

226
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,730
<i>Will Lily Cruz be there?</i>

227
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:56,150
Yes. Lily Cruz will be there.

228
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:59,028
<i>I'll introduce your associate to her.</i>

229
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:01,697
Good. Thank you, Mr. Paterno.

230
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,115
All right. Thanks.

231
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:08,829
We're in.

232
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:14,793
[tense music playing]

233
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:30,851
Jaguar, long time no see.

234
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,353
[distorted voice] What do you want?

235
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:33,854
Why did you call for me?

236
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:35,481
You have an upcoming mission.

237
00:13:35,564 --> 00:13:37,358
The Red Dragon wants you to be ready.

238
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:40,945
Was Red Dragon the one
behind the Aguas Realty bombing?

239
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:42,613
Yes.

240
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:46,325
Why? What does she want from Lily Cruz?

241
00:13:46,825 --> 00:13:48,619
You ask too many questions.

242
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,997
All you need to know right now
is that Red Dragon declared war

243
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:56,252
on Lily Cruz, and she needs
her best lieutenant --you.

244
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:05,094
[soft piano music playing]

245
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:12,351
<i>Your lives are in danger, Camia.</i>

246
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:15,938
<i>I need to save you from the Red Dragon.</i>

247
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:23,070
-[soft piano music playing]
-[water running]

248
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:39,503
[soft piano music playing]

249
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:47,928
Hello, everyone.

250
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:57,146
-Mr. Paterno isn't here?
-He isn't, Miss Cruz.

251
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:59,481
He's in a meeting with the investor today.

252
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:02,318
Meeting with the investor?

253
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:05,112
Did he at least send us
the investor's background?

254
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:08,198
-He didn't.
-He didn't send anything?

255
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,408
Nothing, ma'am.

256
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:14,038
[tense music playing]

257
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:16,582
You may go.

258
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:39,855
[tense music playing]

259
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:05,881
[tense music intensifies]

260
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:09,093
Excuse me. Miss Moran?

261
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:10,886
-Yes.
-Mr. Paterno.

262
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:13,430
-Hi.
-Come with me.

263
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:21,605
She's with me.

264
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:26,026
[line ringing]

265
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,861
[Mercedes] Hello.

266
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:29,738
I'm in now.

267
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:35,953
Good. Blow them up.

268
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:46,005
[suspenseful music playing]

269
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,348
-Mr. Paterno.
-Miss Cruz.

270
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:59,935
Um, I would like you to meet
Miss Mercedes' associate.

271
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:07,943
[suspenseful music playing]

272
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:17,161
[Lily] <i>Diego, do you know that woman?</i>

273
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,287
[Diego] <i>Doesn't she work here?</i>

274
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:20,998
[Lily] <i>I think so. But all alone?</i>

275
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:30,007
-[explosions]
-[screams]

276
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:32,843
You! Stop her!

277
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:35,345
[Lily] Stop her!

278
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:40,100
[suspenseful music playing]

279
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:57,409
[suspenseful music playing]

280
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:02,247
[security officer 1] Hey!

281
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:03,749
[security officer 1] Hey!

282
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:04,583
[grunts]

283
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:05,417
[groans]

284
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:08,921
[grunting]

285
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:14,843
[Lily] Where did she go?

286
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:18,931
[suspenseful music playing]

287
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,477
-Hey!
-[Myla grunts]

288
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:30,234
You… You!

289
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:34,029
You're the one who blew up
the media complex!

290
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,156
That's right! It was me!

291
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:39,618
And I'm here to finish what I started!

292
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:44,414
[action music playing]

293
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:49,545
[both grunting]

294
00:18:57,219 --> 00:19:01,265
[both grunting]

295
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,560
[Lily groans]

296
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:11,108
[both grunting]

297
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:15,696
[grunting]

298
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:30,586
[action music playing]

299
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:33,547
[Myla grunting]

300
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:36,967
[grunting]

301
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:54,234
[screams]

302
00:19:56,320 --> 00:20:01,283
[both grunting]

303
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:08,957
[Myla groans]

304
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:18,091
[both grunting]

305
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:21,970
Where's the bomb? Where's the bomb?!

306
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:26,767
[suspenseful music playing]

307
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:45,202
[suspenseful music intensifies]

308
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,205
[Myla grunts]

309
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:51,583
[both grunting]

310
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:56,588
[grunting continues]

311
00:20:58,757 --> 00:20:59,758
[breathes heavily]

312
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:03,720
[suspenseful music playing]

313
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:22,030
Hello?

314
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:24,449
Call the bomb squad,
and evacuate the building.

315
00:21:24,533 --> 00:21:25,867
Do you understand?

316
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:29,997
Make sure everyone
gets out of this building!

317
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:37,462
[suspenseful music playing]

318
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:43,010
[clamoring]

319
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:47,431
[siren wailing]

320
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:53,812
[clamoring]

321
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:57,190
[all screaming]

322
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:04,406
[suspenseful music intensifies]

323
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:19,755
[bomb timer beeping]

324
00:22:22,883 --> 00:22:25,761
[beeping continues]

325
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:33,560
-[laughs]
-[beeping continues]

326
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:39,524
[suspenseful music playing]

327
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:45,530
-[clamoring]
-[emergency alarm blaring]

328
00:22:46,281 --> 00:22:51,411
-[clamoring]
-[emergency alarm ringing]

329
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:57,501
-[bomb timer beeping]
-[Myla laughing]

330
00:22:57,584 --> 00:22:58,543
[Lily breathes heavily]

331
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:01,880
[bomb timer beeping]

332
00:23:05,383 --> 00:23:07,135
[laughing]

333
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:12,933
-[emergency alarm blaring]
-[clamoring]

334
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:16,228
[bomb timer beeping]

335
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:18,772
[Myla laughing]

336
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:22,275
[breathes heavily]

337
00:23:23,318 --> 00:23:27,531
-[panting]
-[Myla laughing]

338
00:23:27,614 --> 00:23:29,991
-[groans]
-[laughing]

339
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:32,619
[both grunt]

340
00:23:32,702 --> 00:23:35,747
Who do you work for? Who?!

341
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:40,460
Who is the bastard
who ordered you to do this?!

342
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:43,672
[laughing]

343
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:44,714
[Lily groans]

344
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:50,720
[Myla continues laughing]

345
00:23:53,890 --> 00:23:54,975
[indistinct chatter]

346
00:23:58,186 --> 00:23:59,563
[Myla laughing]

347
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:05,569
Make sure that woman doesn't escape.

348
00:24:11,199 --> 00:24:15,203
[Myla laughing]

349
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:19,416
We're here at the main office
of Aguas Realty,

350
00:24:19,499 --> 00:24:23,211
<i>where an alleged</i>
<i>terrorist threat was reported.</i>

351
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:24,713
<i>From what we've gathered,</i>

352
00:24:24,796 --> 00:24:27,424
<i>someone carrying</i>
<i>a bomb infiltrated the building</i>

353
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:29,092
-<i>with the intention of…</i>
-Lily.

354
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:31,553
<i>…blowing Aguas Realty up. As of now,</i>

355
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:35,348
<i>all employees of Aguas Realty</i>
<i>have been evacuated.</i>

356
00:24:35,432 --> 00:24:40,228
<i>And according to reports,</i>
<i>only the CEO, Miss Lily Cruz,</i>

357
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:43,023
<i>is still inside the said building.</i>

358
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:46,401
<i>Just recently, Miss Lily Cruz spoke up</i>

359
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:48,862
<i>regarding the consecutive bombings</i>

360
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:51,281
<i>of Aguas Realty properties,</i>

361
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:55,869
<i>But until now, the person or group</i>

362
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:59,831
<i>behind the bombings is still unidentified.</i>

363
00:25:00,457 --> 00:25:01,666
Well.

364
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:04,044
Looks like karma

365
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:07,255
is a bigger witch
than you are, Miss Lily Cruz.

366
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:12,719
[indistinct chatter]

367
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:17,349
<i>The suspect, who snuck into Aguas Realty</i>

368
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:21,353
<i>with a bomb in her possession,</i>
<i>has now been arrested.</i>

369
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,482
<i>As for Miss Lily Cruz,</i>
<i>she seems unharmed.</i>

370
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,399
[reporters clamor]

371
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:28,360
<i>-Please do the interview later.</i>
<i>-Miss Lily Cruz.</i>

372
00:25:28,443 --> 00:25:29,527
<i>-Make way.</i>
<i>-Miss Lily Cruz.</i>

373
00:25:29,611 --> 00:25:30,946
I thought she was going to die.

374
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:33,031
I thought it was going
to be a happy ending.

375
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:34,866
[cop on TV] <i>Please step aside.</i>

376
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:37,285
[reporter] <i>Miss Lily Cruz!</i>
<i>Your statement, please!</i>

377
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:38,578
Please, stay back.

378
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:40,747
-You can interview them later.
-Miss Lily Cruz!

379
00:25:40,830 --> 00:25:41,998
-Please stay back.
-Miss Lily Cruz!

380
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:43,500
Do you know who's behind this?

381
00:25:43,583 --> 00:25:45,418
<i>Do you know who's behind all this, ma'am?</i>

382
00:25:45,502 --> 00:25:48,380
I wouldn't go against this enemy of yours.

383
00:25:49,005 --> 00:25:51,549
[Julio] I hope he becomes a friend.

384
00:25:52,592 --> 00:25:54,261
As the saying goes…

385
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:58,348
[speaks in Spanish]
"The enemy of my enemy…

386
00:25:59,599 --> 00:26:00,934
is my friend."

387
00:26:01,851 --> 00:26:02,978
[laughs]

388
00:26:06,606 --> 00:26:07,774
[exhales deeply]

389
00:26:14,197 --> 00:26:15,782
[phone ringing]

390
00:26:18,034 --> 00:26:19,494
[phone ringing]

391
00:26:22,163 --> 00:26:24,040
[phone ringing]

392
00:26:27,377 --> 00:26:28,211
Hello?

393
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:30,171
[Anna] <i>Jepoy.</i>

394
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:31,464
Where are you?

395
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,216
I just woke up, Anna.

396
00:26:33,925 --> 00:26:36,303
[sighs] Something happened to Lily.

397
00:26:36,386 --> 00:26:40,307
I know. Uh, I saw the news.

398
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:41,850
I thought you were asleep?

399
00:26:42,726 --> 00:26:47,314
Yes, I was, but I woke up
and saw the news just now.

400
00:26:48,398 --> 00:26:49,149
<i>All right.</i>

401
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:51,985
We're on our way to Lily's
house. You should come too.

402
00:26:52,068 --> 00:26:53,236
Okay, Anna.

403
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,904
<i>I'll talk to you later.</i>
<i>I'll be there, okay?</i>

404
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:57,449
You guys go ahead. I'll meet you there.

405
00:26:58,158 --> 00:26:59,159
Be careful.

406
00:27:03,079 --> 00:27:04,622
[mockingly] "Be careful."

407
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:09,044
[laughs] You're funny.

408
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:11,963
I'll really be careful.

409
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:14,591
And where are you going?

410
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:17,344
I'm going to Anna. They need me.

411
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:23,516
No! You're not going anywhere.
You're staying with me.

412
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:25,101
-Let go of me.
-You're my little puppy dog.

413
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:26,561
Pup--What?!

414
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:31,816
I'm not your little pet!
So, don't strangle me!

415
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:35,111
Use me all you want, but remember this…

416
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:37,572
You can't control me.

417
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,575
-Okay.
-Where's my shirt?

418
00:27:41,201 --> 00:27:44,704
Well, you're so cute. Why are you so mad?

419
00:27:45,288 --> 00:27:47,916
I want you to stay, my little puppy dog.

420
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:49,667
[Natalie] Hmm?

421
00:27:49,751 --> 00:27:52,003
How can I make you stay? Hmm?

422
00:27:53,713 --> 00:27:55,590
How about 10 million pesos?

423
00:27:57,926 --> 00:28:02,472
Ma'am, remember this too.
You can't buy me!

424
00:28:05,558 --> 00:28:06,559
Okay.

425
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:11,272
For each of the heads of the Ardientes?

426
00:28:17,904 --> 00:28:21,825
There you go. Those are
my little puppy dog eyes.

427
00:28:25,453 --> 00:28:27,372
So, what do you say, champion?

428
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:31,084
Will you do that for mommy?

429
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:33,169
Hmm?

430
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:37,298
[tense music playing]

431
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:48,893
Governor, we still have
no intel as to who's responsible

432
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:51,563
for the consecutive bombings
against Aguas Realty.

433
00:28:52,689 --> 00:28:55,316
It's because you're lacking intelligence!

434
00:28:55,608 --> 00:28:57,944
Wait, can you even spell "intelligence"?

435
00:28:58,027 --> 00:29:00,363
You know, I'll give you a bonus.
Spell "smart", instead.

436
00:29:00,655 --> 00:29:05,326
Emilia, will you just please shut up?

437
00:29:05,869 --> 00:29:08,872
Because if you've got nothing
to add to our conversation,

438
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:10,957
keep your trap shut.

439
00:29:11,666 --> 00:29:12,667
Why, Papa?

440
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:14,919
Are you assuming I don't know
anything about this?

441
00:29:16,045 --> 00:29:17,088
Well?

442
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:20,049
Diego, has Lily called you?

443
00:29:20,675 --> 00:29:21,885
Not yet, Auntie.

444
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:25,054
Auntie, don't worry. I'm sure she's safe.

445
00:29:26,556 --> 00:29:27,474
Mom?

446
00:29:28,141 --> 00:29:29,768
-Lily, dear.
-[Diego] Lily.

447
00:29:32,937 --> 00:29:34,814
Lily, are you hurt?

448
00:29:34,898 --> 00:29:36,858
-[Diego] You're wounded.
-It's just a scratch, Mom.

449
00:29:36,941 --> 00:29:38,109
I'm fine.

450
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:39,778
What happened to the bomber?

451
00:29:41,821 --> 00:29:42,864
Diego, do you remember

452
00:29:42,947 --> 00:29:45,617
the woman we saw at the construction site?

453
00:29:45,700 --> 00:29:47,076
-Yeah.
-I was right.

454
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,077
My hunch was right.

455
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:50,371
She was the one who bombed my buildings.

456
00:29:50,663 --> 00:29:53,041
The police have her now
and are interrogating her.

457
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:56,252
I'm sure they'll be
on their way here to update us

458
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:58,713
with whatever information
they can get from her.

459
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:00,757
Who could she be working for?

460
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:04,177
No one else could've done this
except the Ardientes.

461
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:06,763
[tense music playing]

462
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:08,681
[Julio] <i>Oh, really now?</i>

463
00:30:09,015 --> 00:30:13,812
So, you're telling me you know
who's behind all of this?

464
00:30:17,941 --> 00:30:18,942
No.

465
00:30:20,151 --> 00:30:21,611
I rest my case.

466
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:24,489
[Diego] The Ardientes may be violent,

467
00:30:24,572 --> 00:30:26,241
but they don't have any power left.

468
00:30:26,324 --> 00:30:28,618
This isn't new to us, Diego.
They're desperate.

469
00:30:29,285 --> 00:30:32,622
When the Ardientes get crippled,
they become more violent.

470
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:41,589
[tense music playing]

471
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:55,687
Well, what if…

472
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:03,862
[laughs]

473
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:06,197
-What's so funny, Papa?
-[Julio continues laughing]

474
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:10,577
Nothing. It just crossed my mind.

475
00:31:11,286 --> 00:31:17,625
Is it possible that you're
responsible for all this chaos?

476
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:19,544
No, no, no.

477
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:23,715
The thought that your mind can come up

478
00:31:23,798 --> 00:31:27,218
with a plan this big is…

479
00:31:29,095 --> 00:31:34,893
-It's a ridiculous concept!
-[both laughing]

480
00:31:34,976 --> 00:31:38,479
[Julio continues laughing]

481
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:40,273
-[clears throat]
-[Julio laughing]

482
00:31:40,356 --> 00:31:43,776
[laughing continues]

483
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:46,821
[laughs on the inside] <i>Laugh now, Papa.</i>

484
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:50,575
<i>If I'm right in thinking that my</i>
<i>real mother is behind all this,</i>

485
00:31:50,658 --> 00:31:52,368
<i>I'll be the one laughing.</i>

486
00:31:52,452 --> 00:31:54,871
<i>And my laugh will be</i>
<i>even more annoying than yours.</i>

487
00:31:54,954 --> 00:31:58,291
[Julio laughing]

488
00:32:01,961 --> 00:32:04,964
[tense music playing]

489
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:10,511
[Diego] Tea?

490
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:14,641
[soft piano music playing]

491
00:32:15,975 --> 00:32:17,769
I envy Lily and Diego.

492
00:32:17,852 --> 00:32:19,646
They're always there for each other.

493
00:32:22,815 --> 00:32:25,068
It's because Lily can
trust Diego completely

494
00:32:25,151 --> 00:32:27,070
because he's not hiding any secrets.

495
00:32:28,237 --> 00:32:29,572
How can you be so sure?

496
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:44,837
[sighs] Why are you hiding that anyway?

497
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:46,589
What are you talking about?

498
00:32:48,883 --> 00:32:50,301
What exactly is that mark on your neck?

499
00:32:52,053 --> 00:32:53,221
I was shooting a gun.

500
00:32:53,888 --> 00:32:54,847
The bullet bounced back,

501
00:32:54,931 --> 00:32:56,599
and I got burned by the gunpowder.

502
00:32:57,141 --> 00:33:00,603
-Gunpowder, huh? Let me see.
-Mm-hm.

503
00:33:01,270 --> 00:33:04,065
This? You see this?

504
00:33:04,148 --> 00:33:05,483
-What?
-Yeah, right there.

505
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:08,111
You know what, Jepoy? It suits you.

506
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:10,363
But I wish your face were covered in it,

507
00:33:10,446 --> 00:33:12,240
so I'd never see it again.

508
00:33:12,907 --> 00:33:13,866
We already have so many problems.

509
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:15,493
How could you still play around?!

510
00:33:16,369 --> 00:33:18,329
Was it fun? Did it feel good?

511
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:19,622
Huh?

512
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:26,129
[somber music playing]

513
00:33:35,388 --> 00:33:38,307
[somber music playing]

514
00:33:42,895 --> 00:33:44,731
<i>How about 10 million pesos?</i>

515
00:33:45,898 --> 00:33:48,776
<i>For each of the heads of the Ardientes?</i>

516
00:33:57,577 --> 00:33:59,245
I've spoken with the police.

517
00:34:00,955 --> 00:34:04,792
Myla Lomeda, 23 years old.
A resident of Tondo.

518
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:08,004
[sighs] She was on a suicide mission.

519
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:11,466
She risked her life just
so could blow up that building.

520
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:15,178
The police said she still refuses to talk.

521
00:34:15,261 --> 00:34:18,264
But I won't stop until I get information.

522
00:34:18,347 --> 00:34:22,435
I'm going to investigate
and find out who's behind all this.

523
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:29,650
[tense music playing]

524
00:34:35,239 --> 00:34:37,158
Hello, my new friend.

525
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:38,743
How are you?

526
00:34:40,578 --> 00:34:41,913
What do you want, Emilia?

527
00:34:41,996 --> 00:34:45,041
[clicks tongue] I came here
because I wanted to know

528
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:49,128
if Mama had anything to do
with the bombing at Aguas Realty,

529
00:34:49,212 --> 00:34:53,257
and if she had anything
to do with my appointment

530
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:54,967
as the new governor's consultant.

531
00:34:56,636 --> 00:34:59,347
[laughs]

532
00:34:59,430 --> 00:35:01,974
And just why would she do that?

533
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:06,020
[laughing sarcastically]

534
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:08,147
Because I'm her daughter!

535
00:35:08,231 --> 00:35:11,109
If she helped me before,

536
00:35:11,192 --> 00:35:13,945
I'm sure she'd help me again now.

537
00:35:17,657 --> 00:35:20,118
You'll find out soon enough.
When it's the right time.

538
00:35:20,993 --> 00:35:24,539
[tense music playing]

539
00:35:29,418 --> 00:35:30,545
[sighs]

540
00:35:35,716 --> 00:35:37,510
-Hi, Lily, Auntie.
-Hey, Anna.

541
00:35:38,219 --> 00:35:39,595
-I'll get you some food.
-Oh.

542
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:41,973
No need, Auntie. I already ate.
I just dropped by

543
00:35:42,056 --> 00:35:45,935
to let you know I'm off to work
at Lily's teaching program.

544
00:35:46,519 --> 00:35:50,398
Where's Jepoy?
I don't think I saw him leave.

545
00:35:50,481 --> 00:35:52,108
Did he stay here for the night?

546
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:53,734
Oh, just let him be.

547
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:55,945
He was in a bad mood last night
when I talked to him.

548
00:35:56,529 --> 00:35:58,114
He'll come back eventually.

549
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:02,618
Well, in that case, I'll have
my bodyguards go with you.

550
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:03,911
Just to be safe.

551
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:05,746
Okay, Lily. Thanks.

552
00:36:06,455 --> 00:36:08,958
-You sure you won't eat, Anna?
-I'm fine.

553
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,753
Myla still refuses to talk.

554
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:19,051
We can't let things end here.

555
00:36:20,011 --> 00:36:22,054
If that Myla still refuses to talk…

556
00:36:22,805 --> 00:36:24,932
then we'll gather information on our own.

557
00:36:25,474 --> 00:36:27,310
We're going to take the initiative, Diego.

558
00:36:28,644 --> 00:36:31,772
[tense music playing]

559
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:41,199
[Julio laughing]

560
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:44,160
That's what you get for picking on me!

561
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:46,579
[Julio laughing]

562
00:36:46,662 --> 00:36:48,372
-Papa.
-It's a beautiful day!

563
00:36:48,456 --> 00:36:50,791
Good morning! Good morning, Emilia!

564
00:36:50,875 --> 00:36:52,543
It really is a good morning, Papa.

565
00:36:52,627 --> 00:36:53,669
Did you kill someone today?

566
00:36:53,753 --> 00:36:55,338
You've got such a devilish smile.

567
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:57,048
No, no, no. Better!

568
00:36:57,965 --> 00:37:03,763
Someone is messing up Lily Cruz's life!

569
00:37:03,846 --> 00:37:06,349
-[laughs]
-And that can't get any better.

570
00:37:06,432 --> 00:37:07,975
-[laughs] See? See?
-I know.

571
00:37:08,059 --> 00:37:09,518
You're laughing. You're enjoying it.

572
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:11,938
[laughs] I know. It's a really
beautiful day, Papa.

573
00:37:12,021 --> 00:37:13,522
Yes. Okay, let's have breakfast.

574
00:37:13,606 --> 00:37:15,483
Yes. But you're just going to have fruits.

575
00:37:15,566 --> 00:37:16,859
Sir. Ma'am.

576
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:18,236
-Yes?
-Sir Arnaldo's…

577
00:37:18,319 --> 00:37:19,403
gone missing from his room.

578
00:37:20,154 --> 00:37:22,907
How could he go missing?! Find him!

579
00:37:23,658 --> 00:37:24,450
Yes, sir.

580
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:28,037
[suspenseful music playing]

581
00:37:35,795 --> 00:37:40,091
Of all the--Where the hell
did that boy go to now?!

582
00:37:40,675 --> 00:37:44,053
Papa, he could be anywhere. Do something!

583
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:51,018
Governor, we've searched
the premises. He isn't here.

584
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:53,688
I can't accept that.

585
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:56,857
If he's not here, then look outside.

586
00:37:56,941 --> 00:38:00,778
Order all our men to move, if you have to!

587
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:04,657
Governor, we don't have
full access to that, as of now.

588
00:38:04,740 --> 00:38:06,701
I don't care!

589
00:38:07,702 --> 00:38:11,497
I want you to scour every
corner of our province…

590
00:38:12,456 --> 00:38:16,210
before the enemy finds
Arnaldo and kills him!

591
00:38:16,294 --> 00:38:21,841
Enemies like Lily Cruz,
Madrigal, and Diego Torillo!

592
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:24,677
-Yes, sir.
-[Julio] Go!

593
00:38:27,388 --> 00:38:28,514
[sighs]

594
00:38:30,975 --> 00:38:31,976
[groans]

595
00:38:33,060 --> 00:38:34,478
[footsteps departing]

596
00:38:35,187 --> 00:38:36,188
[exhales]

597
00:38:40,568 --> 00:38:41,569
Lily, dear.

598
00:38:41,944 --> 00:38:42,945
Mom?

599
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:46,073
Why not just leave this to the police?

600
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:51,954
I'm sorry, Mom,
but I have to do this myself.

601
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:56,375
Then bring security with you, okay?

602
00:38:57,752 --> 00:38:59,045
We will, Mom.

603
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:04,550
-Be careful.
-Yes, Mom.

604
00:39:04,633 --> 00:39:05,885
-You too, Diego.
-Yes, Auntie.

605
00:39:05,968 --> 00:39:07,803
-We need to go, Mom.
-Okay.

606
00:39:09,889 --> 00:39:10,890
[door opens]

607
00:39:12,975 --> 00:39:14,226
-[door closes]
-[sighs]

608
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,904
[tense music playing]

609
00:39:24,987 --> 00:39:26,739
-[busy tone]
-[sighs]

610
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:28,157
What's wrong with that woman?

611
00:39:28,240 --> 00:39:31,077
Of course she has to be busy
when we actually have to talk.

612
00:39:31,744 --> 00:39:32,745
Annoying.

613
00:39:34,955 --> 00:39:36,165
[busy tone]

614
00:39:36,248 --> 00:39:37,249
Duh!

615
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:39,335
Hmm.

616
00:39:45,966 --> 00:39:48,969
Madam, we cleaned the mess.

617
00:39:49,678 --> 00:39:54,016
[ominous music playing]

618
00:40:05,403 --> 00:40:08,906
[suspenseful music playing]

619
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:21,460
[suspenseful music continues]

620
00:40:26,298 --> 00:40:27,716
Stay here and keep watch.

621
00:40:33,055 --> 00:40:34,056
[door opens]

622
00:40:38,477 --> 00:40:40,354
[suspenseful music intensifies]

623
00:40:53,993 --> 00:40:56,620
[suspenseful music continues]

624
00:41:13,262 --> 00:41:16,348
[suspenseful music continues]

625
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:34,658
[suspenseful music intensifies]

626
00:41:42,625 --> 00:41:45,503
[suspenseful music continues]

627
00:41:58,432 --> 00:42:00,684
[somber music playing]

628
00:42:02,353 --> 00:42:03,437
Diego, don't.

629
00:42:07,316 --> 00:42:08,275
Here.

630
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:22,873
He's dead. He was strangled.

631
00:42:24,875 --> 00:42:27,586
We'll report this to the police
later, anonymously.

632
00:42:28,712 --> 00:42:30,881
But for now, let's hurry up
and find a lead.

633
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:33,509
Okay.

634
00:42:34,718 --> 00:42:37,888
[suspenseful music playing]

635
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:45,646
[door closes]

636
00:42:46,021 --> 00:42:48,232
Well? What's the update?

637
00:42:48,732 --> 00:42:50,317
Sir, we couldn't find him.

638
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:52,528
We've already searched the entire house.

639
00:42:53,487 --> 00:42:56,574
He's not around? Then what
are you still doing here?!

640
00:42:56,657 --> 00:42:58,659
Go out and search for him! Move it!

641
00:43:02,705 --> 00:43:06,292
Papa, I've called my contacts to help.

642
00:43:06,959 --> 00:43:09,837
[laughs]

643
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:14,258
This is a surprise. You have contacts?

644
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:16,051
[Emilia scoffs] Cut it out, Papa!

645
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:20,347
The one time we need to find Arnaldo,
you're basically powerless.

646
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:22,725
And now what? What can you do? Nothing!

647
00:43:22,808 --> 00:43:25,603
-Shut up, Emilia!
-I am not gonna shut up, Papa!

648
00:43:25,686 --> 00:43:28,647
That's the truth!
You are no longer in position,

649
00:43:28,731 --> 00:43:30,858
so that's why you can't do anything now!

650
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:32,985
Papa! Emilia, that's enough!

651
00:43:33,068 --> 00:43:34,028
You know what?

652
00:43:34,111 --> 00:43:37,281
I'll just approach someone
who can truly help us!

653
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:38,574
Hey! Where are you going?!

654
00:43:39,533 --> 00:43:41,243
To Governor Mateo Ruiz.

655
00:43:41,327 --> 00:43:43,579
He's the governor right now, isn't he?

656
00:43:43,662 --> 00:43:45,080
And not you!

657
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:48,584
[tense music playing]

658
00:43:48,667 --> 00:43:49,835
Emilia!

659
00:43:52,296 --> 00:43:54,381
What?! That hurts!

660
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:55,591
[laughs]

661
00:43:58,385 --> 00:43:59,720
[sighs]

662
00:44:04,808 --> 00:44:07,478
[tense music playing]

663
00:44:09,229 --> 00:44:10,230
We can use these.

664
00:44:22,159 --> 00:44:24,870
[tense music playing]

665
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:31,085
Mercedes Palacio?

666
00:44:32,252 --> 00:44:34,838
[tense music intensifies]

667
00:44:38,550 --> 00:44:41,095
[Lily] <i>Mr. Paterno's dead.</i>
<i>We need to be cautious, Mom.</i>

668
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:43,013
<i>I'm not dealing with just anybody here.</i>

669
00:44:43,097 --> 00:44:45,849
<i>But I got a lead. Mercedes Palacio.</i>

670
00:44:45,933 --> 00:44:47,267
[Damian] <i>These people are</i>
<i>on a different level.</i>

671
00:44:47,351 --> 00:44:49,645
<i>-She can't win this.</i>
<i>-Why, Damian?</i>

672
00:44:49,728 --> 00:44:51,730
<i>Do you know Mercedes Palacio?</i>

673
00:44:51,814 --> 00:44:54,525
<i>Find Arnaldo.</i>
<i>Search every corner of Ardiente.</i>

674
00:44:54,608 --> 00:44:55,734
<i>Mayor.</i>

675
00:44:55,818 --> 00:44:58,237
-[grunts] <i>What did I ever do to you?!</i>
<i>-I don't know what--</i>

676
00:44:58,320 --> 00:44:59,905
[Jepoy] <i>Why do you have to hurt</i>
<i>everyone I love?!</i>

677
00:44:59,988 --> 00:45:00,823
[Arnaldo] <i>I don't know you!</i>

678
00:45:00,906 --> 00:45:02,116
[Jepoy] <i>As long as</i>
<i>the Ardientes are around,</i>

679
00:45:02,199 --> 00:45:03,367
<i>our lives are in danger, Diego.</i>

680
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:04,576
[Mercedes] <i>The time has come.</i>

681
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:06,620
<i>Your real mother wants to see you.</i>

682
00:45:06,703 --> 00:45:08,372
[Lily] <i>I've been to hell and back.</i>

683
00:45:08,455 --> 00:45:11,417
<i>There's no way I'll ever be afraid of you!</i>

684
00:45:11,959 --> 00:45:14,420
[theme music playing]
